+
+This patch introduces the following production hardening artifacts:
+- OIDC/JWT validation and RBAC helper (mcp/server/auth.py)
+- Kafka-based durable eventing for MCP (confluent-kafka integration) and a Gatekeeper consumer example
+- Vault HSM/CloudHSM Terraform skeleton and Helm values to use PKCS#11 auto-unseal
+- Rekor monitoring ServiceMonitor & CloudWatch alarm skeletons + backup/restore maintenance
+- GitHub Actions OIDC CI example to remove long-lived secrets and upsert MCP after sign
+- Full SCA workflow (trivy, pip-audit, gosec) in .github
+- Secure-agg: Flower robust aggregator (trimmed mean) + DP post-agg harness
+- Edge pre-load verifier with TPM quote verification placeholder and cosign pubkey pinning
+- OTA fleet rollback validator script to run rollback drills and measure RTO
+- Audit exporter script to stream audit logs to SIEM
+
+Notes:
+- All placeholders (KMS IDs, secrets, domains) MUST be filled with your environment-specific values.
+- HSM/CloudHSM requires coordination with Security vendor; do not deploy without approval.
+- Kafka/Confluent or managed pubsub is recommended for durable events. Basic consumer included as example.
+- JWT validation currently uses python-jose with JWKS fetched from OIDC issuer; in production validate token signatures, verify cti/nonce as applicable.
